VALUES (590, '1', $t$ASK 590: one closing check (the anti-cheat read moved into the closing enforcer), with the send-back$t$,
  $t$The closing-round anti-cheat check is merged into the closing enforcer's two reads, with the send-back, live on every run. (W1's statement of the objective in its grade, Wall 11425; the plan ask589/w3/closing_check_plan.md dad7dfe9; ruling row 516.)$t$,
  'in part',
  $t$Written by W4 on the operator's press of the replacement card at 01:31 CST 2026-11-24 in W4's thread, with no run live (Wall 11448; audit 41285, whose note names the card "Write ASK 590"). Engine moMxiV4Irg1uRBZN a17c7a7b to d819ff4c-059d-438a-96f0-36ca31e93021, 422 nodes; changed: Close Enforcer Build, Close Enforcer Record, Panel Build, Build Independent Verdict, Close Group Batch Build, Send Back Build, Alt Send Back Build, Shared Library; the anti-cheat path leaves the flow and its six nodes stay, reached by nothing. Child MqQHRl7mQQ0z8QdT e9ddab5e to 31329164-efe2-40c9-8791-be855e8025b4; changed: R2 Alt Send Back Build, Shared Library. LIB 8ebbd11e9443b540, MAP 3ae647f38b5b74ac. What is live (card590.md): the closing enforcer's two reads answer each verse a side reads in both its close and its earlier rounds with CONFIRMED, REVERSED READING or NOT A CONTRADICTION. A REVERSED READING stands only when both reads give it, both quotations stand word for word in that side's own rounds, neither is the other side's sentence, and both stand under the same verse; a CONFIRMED contradiction on the same pair wins. Every answer is an E-CLOSECON row of debate_enforcer_log; a reversed reading is not a debater fault. The judges are shown the block [REVERSED CLOSE SENTENCES] in place of the [ANTI-CHEAT CHECK] notes. A judge line that quotes 8 or more words in a row of a reversed close sentence goes back once as E-REVCLOSE; the judge keeps the decision (ruling 428); the item is not counted against any seat. Ruling 427's rule is kept and its TRIAL status ends. No new model call. The path: plan draft graded PASS with F1 and F2 (Wall 11389); the operator's press "Build it, with the send-back" (row 516); build rev 0 (Wall 11424), W1 PASS (Wall 11425); re-cut on the ASK 593 write (Wall 11444), W1 PASS (Wall 11446); the write (Wall 11448); W1 readback MATCH (Wall 11449). IN PART, for two reasons. (1) No run has executed on d819ff4c or any later version: the proofs are offline replays, and every REVERSED answer in them is planted, because no model REVERSED answer is stored anywhere (card590.md section 4). How many REVERSED READING findings a live read gives is measured on the first run. (2) DEFECT OF THIS WRITE, found by W1 after its readback (Wall 11452): the E-REVCLOSE matcher (library line 3564, rev590Hits) recorded the judge's line cut to 1,500 characters, and the three send-back builders stored it as flagged_line and response_line with no mark. That is the ASK 587 item A defect again, in code W1 graded and W4 built; both stated it as their mistake (Wall 11452, 11453), and W3's plan did not name ASK 587 item A as a check. Corrected by ASK 595 (its own row). Also found then and not part of this row: the block's quotations are shown cut to 500 characters and the send-back text's to 400 (Wall 11453, 11456). Size: each enforcer read grows from 55,463 to 98,345 characters up to 189,872 (Wall 11424 item 6). Correction to the record made by the build: run 42071 holds ONE confirmed closing contradiction, not 3 (Wall 11424 item 5). Left standing by this write: the six Anticheat nodes, unreached (ASK 598 plans their removal).$t$,
  '11389, 11424, 11425, 11444, 11446, 11448, 11449, 11452',
  current_setting('truth.session_id'), NULL,
  to_jsonb($t$00:25 CST 2026-11-24, W3 thread, press "Build it, with the send-back" on the card "Approve W4 building the single closing check (ASK 590)?" (ruling row 516). His earlier words on the anti-cheat check, 23:45 CST 2026-11-23, W3 thread (ruling row 513): "A2 is something i requested.. tell me what it does?" The write press: the replacement card in W4's thread, 01:31 CST 2026-11-24 (Wall 11448; audit 41285).$t$::text),
  $j${"answer": "not in the record W3 read (audit 41285 names the card \"Write ASK 590\" (replacement))", "source": "Wall 11448; audit 41285", "thread": "W4", "press_time": "01:31 CST 2026-11-24", "question": "not in the record W3 read (the card is in W4's thread); the card text is ask590/w4/card590.md c8bb6c73"}$j$::jsonb,
  'W4',
  $j${"md5": "dad7dfe9", "path": "ask589/w3/closing_check_plan.md", "commit": "dc713a4a", "note": "W3's plan; draft 1 9050ce8d graded PASS with F1 and F2 (Wall 11389); dad7dfe9 is the version the operator's build press names (row 516)", "source": "md5sum by W3; ruling row 516; Wall 11389"}$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[{"md5": "abb0e221", "path": "ask590/w4/recut593/target_engine_590s.json", "note": "the engine as re-cut on live a17c7a7b; graded (Wall 11446), written and read back", "source": "md5sum by W3; Wall 11446, 11449"}, {"md5": "82073ba9", "path": "ask590/w4/recut593/target_child_590s.json", "note": "the child as re-cut on live e9ddab5e", "source": "md5sum by W3; Wall 11446, 11449"}, {"md5": "91de1679", "path": "ask590/w4/build/target_engine_590s.json", "note": "the first target, on base 9bec145c; graded (Wall 11425, which states this md5); not written", "source": "md5sum by W3; Wall 11425"}, {"md5": "fd127191", "path": "ask590/w4/build/target_child_590s.json", "note": "the first child target, on base 2d5bdc94; graded (Wall 11425 states this md5); not written", "source": "md5sum by W3; Wall 11425"}, {"md5": "755d4d9b", "path": "ask590/w4/build590_notes.md", "note": "build notes rev 0, commit 56ffa5ed", "source": "md5sum by W3; Wall 11424"}, {"md5": "c8bb6c73", "path": "ask590/w4/card590.md", "note": "the card text, with the re-cut note", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "189d455c", "path": "ask590/w4/recut593/build590.cjs", "note": "the build script, layer 1 (differs from the graded build in its base check alone, Wall 11446)", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "4b83cb8e", "path": "ask590/w4/recut593/build590_l2.cjs", "note": "the build script, layer 2 (the send-back)", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "e162123c", "path": "ask590/w4/recut593/t590.cjs", "note": "test, 26 cases", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "6cbc1cd6", "path": "ask590/w4/recut593/t590s.cjs", "note": "test, 25 cases", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "321a71e7", "path": "ask590/w4/recut593/t590rec.cjs", "note": "test, 6 cases", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "adf441e9", "path": "ask590/w4/recut593/t590r.cjs", "note": "test, 9 replays", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "9d4dfe5a", "path": "ask590/w4/write_r593/prewrite_eng590.json", "note": "fresh fetch before the write; the same md5 as recut593/base_eng.json and ask593's fetchback_eng593.json", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "644ce589", "path": "ask590/w4/write_r593/prewrite_child590.json", "note": "fresh fetch before the write, child", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "2c766aca", "path": "ask590/w4/write_r593/put_eng590.json", "note": "PUT body, engine", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "825398a7", "path": "ask590/w4/write_r593/put_child590.json", "note": "PUT body, child", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "10b2bcc8", "path": "ask590/w4/write_r593/fetchback_eng590.json", "note": "fetch-back after the write", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "26a0a881", "path": "ask590/w4/write_r593/fetchback_child590.json", "note": "fetch-back after the write, child", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "1c3cf1e9", "path": "ask590/w4/write_r593/write590r.sh", "note": "the write script", "source": "md5sum by W3"}]$j$::jsonb,
  $j${"copy": "restore the engine and the child together from ask590/w4/write_r593/revert_eng590.json 2299aa0b and revert_child590.json 9364397d (to a17c7a7b and e9ddab5e). A revert now would also undo ASK 595, 586 J1 and 586 J6, which were written on top.", "path": "ask590/w4/write_r593/revert_eng590.json; ask590/w4/write_r593/revert_child590.json", "source": "Wall 11448 item 4; md5sum by W3; the last sentence is W3's reading of the chain in Wall 11485"}$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[{"seat": "W1", "verdict": "PASS (re-cut on the ASK 593 write: W1's rebuild equals W4's re-cut targets and the 593_on590 targets, 0 differences; t590 26, t590s 25, t590rec 6, t590r 9 PASS; Library pair PASSES)", "wall_id": 11446, "md5_graded": "abb0e221", "verdict_norm": "PASS", "source": "Wall 11446 item (1); the md5 is md5sum by W3 on ask590/w4/recut593/target_engine_590s.json; W1's post names the commit 56ffa5ed, not this md5"}, {"seat": "W1", "verdict": "PASS (the re-cut child target, the same grade)", "wall_id": 11446, "md5_graded": "82073ba9", "verdict_norm": "PASS", "source": "Wall 11446 item (1); md5sum by W3 on ask590/w4/recut593/target_child_590s.json"}, {"seat": "W1", "verdict": "PASS (build rev 0 on base 9bec145c and 2d5bdc94; rulings asked R1, R2, R3 ACCEPTED; \"Write not counted, not record-only, on the card and in the manual\")", "wall_id": 11425, "md5_graded": "91de1679", "verdict_norm": "PASS", "source": "Wall 11425: \"my rebuild gives engine 91de1679 and child fd127191 exactly\""}, {"seat": "W1", "verdict": "PASS (build rev 0, the child target)", "wall_id": 11425, "md5_graded": "fd127191", "verdict_norm": "PASS", "source": "Wall 11425"}, {"seat": "W1", "verdict": "PASS with F1 and F2 (the plan, draft 1 9050ce8d)", "wall_id": 11389, "md5_graded": "9050ce8d", "verdict_norm": "PASS", "source": "Wall 11389 head"}]$j$::jsonb,
  ARRAY['abb0e221','82073ba9'], '[41285]'::jsonb,
  $j$[{"kind": "n8n workflow", "name": "ORACLE_DEBATE_V1 moMxiV4Irg1uRBZN", "before": "a17c7a7b, 422 nodes", "after": "d819ff4c-059d-438a-96f0-36ca31e93021, 422 nodes"}, {"kind": "n8n workflow", "name": "child MqQHRl7mQQ0z8QdT", "before": "e9ddab5e, 156 nodes", "after": "31329164-efe2-40c9-8791-be855e8025b4, 156 nodes"}, {"kind": "n8n nodes, changed (8 engine, 2 child)", "name": "engine: Close Enforcer Build, Close Enforcer Record, Panel Build, Build Independent Verdict, Close Group Batch Build, Send Back Build, Alt Send Back Build, Shared Library; child: R2 Alt Send Back Build, Shared Library", "before": "as in a17c7a7b and e9ddab5e", "after": "as in the targets (Wall 11448 items 1 and 2)"}, {"kind": "n8n connections", "name": "the anti-cheat path", "before": "in the flow", "after": "out of the flow: Check Save and Regrade After Quotes? go to Panel Build; Close Enforcer Build goes to Assume Check Build; the six Anticheat nodes are reached by nothing (Wall 11425)"}, {"kind": "library", "name": "Shared Library, engine and child", "before": "LIB a5b27df14d596da7, MAP e6f0341b87c6190c (row 160)", "after": "LIB 8ebbd11e9443b540, MAP 3ae647f38b5b74ac"}]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[{"name": "t590 (26), t590s (25), t590rec (6), t590r (9 replays): 66 offline tests", "result": "66 PASS at the build, at W1's rerun, on the re-cut and at the write", "source": "Wall 11424 item 3; 11425; 11444; 11446; 11448 item 3"}, {"name": "Library Check pair", "result": "PASSES: LIB 8ebbd11e9443b540, MAP 3ae647f38b5b74ac", "source": "Wall 11446; 11448 item 3"}, {"name": "Replays on stored runs 32643, 41822, 37203, 42071", "result": "32643: the defender's Deuteronomy 22:24 is a candidate; 41822: the crossed note is not raised; 37203: the wrong-verse pairing is refused; 42071: its one confirmed contradiction is unchanged. The REVERSED answers are planted.", "source": "card590.md section 4; Wall 11424 items 4 and 5"}, {"name": "NOT TESTED: ASK 587 item A (a judge line over 1,500 characters stored and shown whole)", "result": "not among the 66 tests; the write cut the E-REVCLOSE line at 1,500", "source": "Wall 11452 (W1's mistake stated), 11453 (W4's mistake stated)"}]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[{"seat": "W1", "wall_id": 11449, "result": "MATCH (W1's own fetch: engine d819ff4c, 422 nodes, equals recut593/target_engine_590s.json and W1's rebuild, 0 node differences, connections equal; child 31329164, 156 nodes, the same)"}]$j$::jsonb,
  $j${"case": "UNEXERCISED. No run has executed on d819ff4c or a later version (debate_results last row 03:57 UTC 2026-11-24, run 42071; Wall 11483, 11485). EXPECT on the first run: debate_enforcer_log holds E-CLOSECON rows with the answers CONFIRMED, REVERSED READING or NOT A CONTRADICTION; no judge request holds [ANTI-CHEAT CHECK]; a REVERSED READING appears to the judges under [REVERSED CLOSE SENTENCES]; any E-REVCLOSE item is sent back once and counts against no seat; no Anticheat node executes.", "source": "card590.md sections 1 and 2; Wall 11448; the EXPECT list is W3's reading of the card, not a statement of W4's"}$j$::jsonb,
  $j${"op_doc": "none", "engine_manual": "not yet at the draft of this row: version 287 (9f39e989). W3's entries for ASK 590, 595, 586 J1 and 586 J6 are manual1123/w3/a590_595_586/em_pairs_590_595_586_draft2.json b3ed7178 (8 parts, 11 pairs), W1 PASS (Wall 11488, 11491), on the operator's card, not pressed at the draft of this row"}$j$::jsonb,
